{
  "title": "Make committed pipeline reports deterministic across machines",
  "description": "With AI enrichments removed from pipeline snapshots \
(follow-up to p2-remove-ai-enrichments-from-pipeline-snapshots), snapshots are \
now fully deterministic given the scrape cache — but several committed data/ \
reports still churn whenever two machines have different ~/.ramekin/ai-cache \
contents:\n\
\n\
- data/tag-report.md is entirely AI-derived, so any cache miss rewrites it.\n\
- data/extraction-report.md's 'AI Cache' hit/miss counts and 'Completed' \
counts vary with per-machine cache state (enrichment failures count against \
completion), even though extraction itself is deterministic.\n\
- The title-normalization and description-generation eval reports under data/ \
have the same property.\n\
\n\
Every `make pipeline` run on a machine with a cold or different AI cache \
produces large spurious diffs in these files (e.g. ~1000 changed lines in \
tag-report.md), which drowns out the meaningful extraction/parsing diffs \
reviewers actually need to see. Decide per report whether to (a) stop \
committing it, (b) split the AI-dependent sections into an uncommitted report, \
or (c) make the counts cache-independent (e.g. report extraction completion \
separately from enrichment success).",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 3,
  "type": "task",
  "labels": [
    "pipeline",
    "ai",
  ],
